    "title": "Photos: Stormy weather impacts daily routines in Beaumont - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kim Brent ,\n4 hours ago Shoppers and outside store workers wait out another round of heavy rainfall and thunder outside the Kroger on Phelan Boulevard Wednesday afternoon. Photo made Wednesday, September 24, 2025 Kim Brent/Beaumont Enterprise staff (Kim Brent) Rounds of heavy rain and thunderstorms ping-ponged their way throughout the afternoon Wednesday, disrupting Southeast Texans’ work and daily chores.\nThe storms moved in ahead of a cold front expected to arrive in the region late Wednesday, bringing lightning, thunder and bouts of very heavy rain that already were causing some roadways to pick up standing water throughout the day.\nRELATED: Storms expected ahead of cold front and beyond\nShoppers and workers alike were impacted at several area stores, including the Kroger on Phelan Boulevard, where both waited out the heavy rain before continuing on with their day.\nCheck back tomorrow morning for a preview of Thursday’s forecast.\nSign up for Beaumont Enterprise newsletters here\nRead the original article on beaumontenterprise.com",
